_48h": 0, "first_news_at": null, "news_before_x": false, "top_domains": [], "covered": true, "lean_mix": {"L": 0, "C": 0, "R": 0, "?": 0, "rated": 0, "texas": 0, "one_sided": null}, "checked_at": "2026-10-16T19:30+00:00"}, "id": 1, "text": "Social safety nets are failing in many areas of America because of the rapidly rising cost of living.", "type": "fact", "checkable": true, "stance": "neutral", "entities": [], "verdict": "misleading", "verdict_basis": "- Strain is real, but the cause is mixed. CPR (Colorado), Billy Penn (Philadelphia) and Capital B Atlanta report food banks under pressure. They blame \ncuts in federal food assistance and a rise in the cost of living\n together. CPBP data cited by Capital B shows \nnational SNAP participation fell by 4 million from July 2025 to March 2026\n after the July 2025 federal law. So the claim's single cause, cost of living, leaves out a policy cause that the same reporting stresses.\n- \"Rapidly rising\" is only partly right. BLS data reported by CNBC shows \nannual inflation of 3.7% in September\n, which is up from 3.4% in August and driven largely by gasoline. Core CPI was \n2.6%\n, and shelter inflation was 3.2% per Trading Economics. In Texas, the Texas Real Estate Research Center found \nstatewide prices 0.2 percent below year-ago levels, with a median of $339,000, unchanged from last year\n. Affordability is still poor. NLIHC reports \nonly 26 rental homes affordable and available for every 100 extremely low-income households\n, and the TAAHP survey found \n54% of Texans say housing affordability is getting worse in their community\n. That is a high level of housing cost, not a sharp recent rise in", "verdict_sources": ["https://www.cpr.org/2026/10/15/snap-cuts-food-banks-families/", "https://billypenn.com/2026/05/18/snap-cuts-philly-food-banks-strained/", "https://atlanta.capitalbnews.org/atlanta-food-bank-demand-surges-black-families/", "https://www.cnbc.com/2026/10/14/cpi-inflation-report-september-2026.html", "https://trerc.tamu.edu/reports/texas-housing-insight-september-2026/", "https://nlihc.org/sites/default/files/SHP_TX.pdf", "https://taahp.org/build-texas-report-survey-shows-majority-of-texans-say-housing-costs-are-getting-worse-want-action-from-lawmakers-to-address-affordability/"], "posts": 1, "views": 126040, "accounts": 1, "copies": 0, "pushback_posts": 0, "lanes": [{"key": "housing_first_funding", "label": "Fund housing-first, not criminalization", "color": "#e66767", "posts": 1}], "first_seen": "2026-10-11T20:56:43+00:00", "first_handle": "yt:UCaXkIU1QidjPwiAYu6GcHjg", "first_handles": ["yt:UCaXkIU1QidjPwiAYu6GcHjg"], "first_url": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=wjoTld1S8os", "first_source": "yt", "first_name": "MS NOW", "sources": {"yt": {"posts": 1, "views": 126040, "engagement": 3014, "first_seen": "2026-10-11T20:56:43+00:00", "first_handle": "yt:UCaXkIU1QidjPwiAYu6GcHjg", "first_url": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=wjoTld1S8os"}}, "cross_platform": false, "platform_lag_h": null, "first_views": 126040, "last_seen": "2026-10-11T20:56:43+00:00", "views_24h": 0, "series": [["2026-10-11T20:56:43+00:00", 126040]], "top_post": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=wjoTld1S8os"}, {"event": null, "event_type": null, "news": {"articles": 2, "sources": 2, "sources_48h": 0, "articles_48h": 0, "first_news_at": "2026-10-11T20:30:05+00:00", "news_before_x": false, "top_domains": ["yahoo.com", "ms.now"], "covered": true, "lean_mix": {"L": 1, "C": 0, "R": 0, "?": 1, "rated": 1, "texas": 0, "one_sided": null}, "checked_at": "2026-10-16T19:30+00:00"}, "id": 2, "text": "A mother of four was thrown out of a homeless shelter in Maricopa County despite her efforts.", "type": "fact", "checkable": true, "stance": "neutral", "entities": ["Maricopa County"], "verdict": "supported", "verdict_basis": "The claim's wording matches the title of an MS NOW segment from \"The Assignment with Antonia Hylton\", which was posted around October 11, 2026. The segment \nfeatures Marshae Jenkins, a mother of four who is getting help from AZ Hugs after she and her family were thrown out of a homeless shelter\n. The segment's text says \nAZ Hugs founder Austin Davis helps families in Maricopa County\n. A description of the segment says she is \ncurrently living in a motel in Arizona\n. ProPublica's reporting from the same week shows the wider setting. \nFamily homelessness in Maricopa County has risen to its highest level in more than a decade, while every shelter is full and housing vouchers are scarce.\n I found no record of the shelter's reason for removing her, and \"despite her efforts\" is the segment's framing of her own account. I could not check the underlying facts independently. Maricopa County is in Arizona, not Texas, so the claim is accurate as worded but has nothing to do with Texas policy. Some reposts also label the clip as NBC, but the original is MS NOW.", "verdict_sources": ["https://www.ms.now/the-assignment/watch/mother-of-four-thrown-out-of-homeless-shelter-despite-her-efforts-it-s-an-epidemic-2516992579599", "https://www.propublica.org/article/maricopa-county-homeless-hub-hotline-shelters", "https://www.radiofree.org/2026/10/09/an-arizona-countys-housing-hub-is-a-dead-end-for-many-homeless-families/"], "posts": 1, "views": 126040, "accounts": 1, "copies": 0, "pushback_posts": 0, "lanes": [{"key": "housing_first_funding", "label": "Fund housing-first, not criminalization", "color": "#e66767", "posts": 1}], "first_seen": "2026-10-11T20:56:43+00:00", "first_handle": "yt:UCaXkIU1QidjPwiAYu6GcHjg", "first_handles": ["yt:UCaXkIU1QidjPwiAYu6GcHjg"], "first_url": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=wjoTld1S8os", "first_source": "yt", "first_name": "MS NOW", "sources": {"yt": {"posts": 1, "views": 126040, "engagement": 3014, "first_seen": "2026-10-11T20:56:43+00:00", "first_handle": "yt:UCaXkIU1QidjPwiAYu6GcHjg", "first_url": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=wjoTld1S8os"}}, "cross_platform": false, "platform_lag_h": null, "first_views": 126040, "last