ive in America.", "type": "fact", "checkable": true, "stance": "against", "entities": [], "verdict": "unsupported", "verdict_basis": "NAR's 2026 International Transactions report (published July 29, 2026) counts \n67,100 foreign-buyer purchases of existing homes between April 2025 and March 2026, the second-lowest level since NAR began tracking in 2009\n. That is \nabout 1.7% of existing-home purchases\n. \nMost of those purchases (37,600, or 56%) were by recent immigrants or visa holders already living in the U.S.\n, so buyers based abroad were fewer still. In Texas, \n12% of foreign purchasers bought there\n, and the Texas Tribune's coverage of the comptroller's report describes \na bipartisan consensus that affordability problems stem from a shortage of homes\n. The Comptroller's report points to \nsupply that hasn't kept up with demand\n, \nhigher interest rates\n and \nzoning and land-use rules that limit development\n. Newsweek's reporting likewise says \nsupply, construction levels, zoning and mortgage rates are much larger drivers of affordability than foreign ownership\n. Foreign buyers can affect prices in some local markets, but a share this small does not support calling them \"the reason\" homes are expensive nationally. One caveat is that NAR's figures come from a member survey and may be imperfect.", "verdict_sources": ["https://www.nar.realtor/newsroom/foreign-buyers-purchased-45-3-billion-worth-of-u-s-homes-from-april-25-to-march-26", "https://www.worldpropertyjournal.com/real-estate-news/united-states/miami-real-estate-news/2026-foreign-home-buyer-data-national-association-of-realtor-2026-international-transactions-in-us-residential-real-estate-report-lawrence-yun-14829.php", "https://usalendingandrealty.com/foreign-buyers-retreat-from-u-s-housing/", "https://www.texastribune.org/2024/08/27/texas-comptroller-housing-shortage-affordability/", "https://www.newsweek.com/foreign-buyers-flee-u-s-housing-but-it-wont-help-american-buyers-12263188", "https://qz.com/foreign-home-buyers-2026", "https://www.bisnow.com/news/dallas-ft-worth/construction-development/texas-housing-abhr-studiob-126972"], "posts": 1, "views": 74093, "accounts": 1, "copies": 0, "pushback_posts": 0, "lanes": [{"key": "investors_developers_blame", "label": "Blame investors, landlords, developers", "color": "#c98500", "posts": 1}], "first_seen": "2026-10-16T15:44:58+00:00", "first_handle": "WallStreetApes", "first_handles": ["WallStreetApes"], "first_url": "https://x.com/WallStreetApes/status/2111121230980149384", "first_source": "x", "first_name": "Wall Street Apes", "sources": {"x": {"posts": 1, "views": 74093, "engagement": 4681, "first_seen": "2026-10-16T15:44:58+00:00", "first_handle": "WallStreetApes", "first_url": "https://x.com/WallStreetApes/status/2111121230980149384"}}, "cross_platform": false, "platform_lag_h": null, "first_views": 74093, "last_seen": "2026-10-16T15:44:58+00:00", "views_24h": 74093, "series": [["2026-10-16T15:44:58+00:00", 74093]], "top_post": "https://x.com/WallStreetApes/status/2111121230980149384"}, {"event": null, "event_type": null, "news": {"articles": 0, "sources": 0, "sources_48h": 0, "articles_48h": 0, "first_news_at": null, "news_before_x": false, "top_domains": [], "covered": true, "lean_mix": {"L": 0, "C": 0, "R": 0, "?": 0, "rated": 0, "texas": 0, "one_sided": null}, "checked_at": "2026-10-16T19:31+00:00"}, "id": 5, "text": "A La Quinta hotel room in Dallas costs about $60 per night.", "type": "fact", "checkable": true, "stance": "neutral", "entities": ["La Quinta", "Dallas"], "verdict": null, "verdict_basis": null, "verdict_sources": [], "posts": 1, "views": 52919, "accounts": 1, "copies": 0, "pushback_posts": 1, "lanes": [{"key": "pushback", "label": "Pushback", "color": "#199e70", "posts": 1}], "first_seen": "2026-10-15T16:10:41+00:00", "first_handle": "TheMindScourge", "first_handles": ["TheMindScourge"], "first_url": "https://x.com/TheMindScourge/status/2110765313176596686", "first_source": "x", "fir